    "product-detail-faq": {
      "type": "product-detail-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "a7b801b0-a37e-4794-b888-ad81c42746e6": {
          "type": "FAQ",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Q: I purchased two Jackery items (Explorer 1000+Saga 100W), why did I just receive one package? Where is my stuff?",
            "content": "<p>1. Your purchase order (including purchases on Solar Generator Bundles) will be shipped separately if the order contains more than one item. This shipping rule is additionally applicable for Amazon orders.<br/>2. You can only find one tracking number in your order even if the order contains more than one package. We are pleased to email you with all tracking numbers when requested.<br/>3. Please feel free to contact us through this email address: hello@Jackery.com or via Amazon.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ef7d6ff7-2235-4ef3-bdb6-a4a3edf33508": {
          "type": "FAQ",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Q: What is the maximum watts of solar panels can be used to charge Explorer 1000? Also how long will it take to recharge from a fully discharge batery?",
            "content": "<p>A: The maximum input wattage of Explorer 1000 is 200w(12~30V,7.5~8.33A ). As for recharging time, it depends on which panel you are using and weather conditions, for example, the Explorer 1000 can be quickly recharged within 8 hours by connecting two SolarSaga 100W solar panels together with an adapter cable. If connecting only one single panel, the approximate recharging time is 17 hours. Recharging time may varies from different location, temperature, weather etc, the actual time may be different.</p>"
          }
        },
        "32cb2a1e-80bc-433d-aac8-446cad50d9bb": {
          "type": "FAQ",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Q: What devices can Explorer 1000 power?",
            "content": "<p>A: Please note that the AC output ports can only charge/power devices that operate at less than 1000-Watts, besides, the whole wattage should be under 1000 watts as well . Once exceeding, the Explorer 1000 will shut off automatically. Please refer to your device specification before purchase.</p>"
          }
        },
        "aff94ce1-1367-4afe-b388-2feff3284841": {
          "type": "FAQ",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Q: How to know the working times for my device?",
            "content": "<p>Working time = 1002Wh* 0.85 / operating wattage of your device<br/>For reference, assuming power consumption of your device is 60W (might be a box fan), working time will be 1002Wh*0.85/60w=14.2hrs (rough calculated).<br/>Please note: actual power consumption varies from different usages, please consult Jackery for better purchase decision.</p>"
          }
        },
        "c6473f8e-8164-47c8-9d9b-dcf9e7927431": {
          "type": "FAQ",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Q: Is the Explorer 1000 power station waterproof?",
            "content": "<p>A: The Explorer 1000 is not waterproof. Please do not store them in humid environment for longtime.</p>"
          }
        },
        "9823965f-42b2-465d-ba23-60f987c9e2f5": {
          "type": "FAQ",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Q: Can the Explorer 1000 be charged while using?",
            "content": "<p>A: Yes, you can use the Explorer 1000 to charge devices, while it's being re-charged at the same time.</p>"
          }
        },
        "d682f26c-43c8-4346-aa8d-14fed4e97711": {
          "type": "FAQ",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Q: Is the solar panel waterproof?",
            "content": "<p>A: The Saga 100W is not waterproof. To maximize the lifespan of the module,Please don’t make it get wet.</p>"
          }
        },
        "818d1072-3590-4e0b-b92a-2272a9cef961": {
          "type": "FAQ",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Q: Why the solar can not produce 100W power when charging to Explorer 1000 power station?",
            "content": "<p>A: As you know , the solar panels are affected by many factors, such as the intensity of the light and the angle of the panel put on the ground. 100W is tested in an ideal laboratory. However, the intensity of the light constantly changes. In addition, the angle of the light illuminating the solar panel also changes with the rotation of the sun. Please try test your solar panel under the full sunlight to see, and make sure there is no shadow cast on the panel.</p>"
          }
        },
        "cb0a5744-a91e-4705-9a5a-704894514e35": {
          "type": "FAQ",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Q: How to clean the solar panel surface?",
            "content": "<p>A: We mentioned this point in the manual. Please use a soft cloth to remove the dust and dirt on the surface. Use a damp cloth to wipe the surface of the solar module to remove any remaining dust or dirt. Any guano or other adhesive should be removed as soon as possible from the solar surface to avoid a reduction in performance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ee3a32df-cfcb-492e-85b6-0cb9044f1cbb": {
          "type": "FAQ",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Q: Can the solar panel charge smartphones and tablet?",
            "content": "<p>A: Yes, the 100W solar panel has 1* USB-C(5V,3A) output port and 1* USB-A(5V, 2.4A) output port.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
